{"id":"word:hebrew:H7069","type":"word","title":"קָנָה","subtitle":"H7069 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to erect , i.e. create ; by extension, to procure , especially by purchase (causatively, sell ); by implication to own","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to קָנָה (H7069) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 86 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"קָנָה (qânâh) means to erect , i.e. create ; by extension, to procure , especially by purchase (causatively, sell ); by implication to own First listed occurrence: 1Chr 21 24."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"קָנָה","transliteration":"qânâh","pronunciation":"kaw-naw'","strong":"H7069","lemmaId":"hebrew:H7069","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["קְנֵ֣ה","וַ/יִּ֜קֶן","וְ/לִ/קְנ֤וֹת","וַ/יִּ֨קֶן","קָנִ֨יתִי֙"],"morphs":[["HVqv2ms",12],["HR/Vqc",6],["HVqp3ms",6],["HVqp1cs",6],["HVqp2ms",6],["HC/Vqw3ms",4],["HVqa",3],["HVqrmsa",3],["HTd/Vqrmsa",3],["HVqi3ms",3]]},"definitions":{"short":"to erect , i.e. create ; by extension, to procure , especially by purchase (causatively, sell ); by implication to own","usage":"attain, buy(-er), teach to keep cattle, get, provoke to jealousy, possess(-or), purchase, recover, redeem, × surely, × verily.","full":"H7069. qanah I. קָנָה 84 verb get, acquire (Late Hebrew = Biblical Hebrew; Phoenician (Punic) מקנא , property [in cattle]; Assyrian ‡anû , gain , acquire , Meissn Suppl. 85 ; Arabic (,) acquire, procure ; Sabean קני acquire, possess , CIS iv,no.89, 5.6 , קני noun property Id ib,no.3, 8, 29, 3 ; Ethiopic acquire, subjugate ; Aramaic קְנָא , ( accquire ); — Qal 81 Perfect 3masculine singular ׳ק Gen 25:10 +; suffix נ֑ךָ קֶָ Deut 32:6 , קָנָהוּ Lev 27:24 ; 3 feminine singular קָֽנְתָה Psa 78:54 ; 2 masculine singular קָנִיתָ Exod 15:16 +, etc.; Imperfect 3masculine singular יִקְנֶךְ Lev 22:11 +, וַיִ֫קֶן Gen 33:19 +, etc.; Imperative masculine singular קְנֵח 47:19 +; Infinitive absolute קָנֹה Lev 25:14 ; 1Chr 21:24 , קָנוֺ 2Sam 24:24 ; cstr . קְנֹה Prov 16:16 , קְנוֺת 16:16 +, etc.; Participle קֹנֶה Deut 28:68 , קְוֺנֶה Prov 15:32 +, etc.; — 1 get, acquire (all poetry) : a. of God as originating, creating , וָאָרֶץ שָׁמַיִם קֹנֵה Gen 14:19 , 22 ; Deut 32:6 (Israel), Psa 139:13 ( כִּלְֹיתָ֑י ); Prov 8:22 ( חכמה q. v.). b. of God as victoriously redeeming his people Exod 15:16 ; Isa 11:11 ; Psa 74:2 (|| גָּאַל ) object הַרוֶֿה 78:54 . c. of Eve, acquiring ׳אֶתיֿ קַיִן, (i.e. with the help of ), Gen 4:1 (J). d. of acquiring wisdom, knowledge (only Proverbs): Prov 1:5 ; 4:5 (twice in verse); 4:7 (twice in verse); 15:32 ; 16:16 (twice in verse); 17:16 ; 18:15 ; 19:8 ; 23:23 . 2 elsewhere buy Exod 21:2 (E), Gen 47:22 (J), 50:13 (P), Lev 27:24 (H), Deut 28:68 ; Isa 24:2 ; Jer 13:1 ; Ezek 7:12 ; Prov 20:14 +; קֹנֶה owner , as purchaser Lev 25:30 (P) Isa 1:3 ; Zech 11:5 +. Niph`al be bought : Perfect 3masculine singular נִקְנָה Jer 32:43 ; Imperfect 3masculine plural יִקָּנוּ 32:15 . Hiph`il Perfect 3masculine singular suffix חִקְנַנִי אָדָם Zech 13:5 ; AV makes denominative of מִקְנֶה cattle ; Thes RV Marti Kau Buhl caused (one) to purchase me , i.e. made me a bondman ; &lt; We Now GASm read קִנְיָנִי אֲרָמָה — Participle מַקְנֶה see קנא .","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 21 24","keyReferences":["1Chr 21 24","1Chr 21 24","1Kgs 16 24","2Chr 34 11","2Kgs 12 13","2Kgs 22 6","2Sam 12 3","2Sam 24 21"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":86,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 21 24","book":"1Chr","chapter":21,"verse":24,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"קָנֹ֥ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqa"},{"reference":"1Chr 21 24","book":"1Chr","chapter":21,"verse":24,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֶקְנֶ֖ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqi1cs"},{"reference":"1Kgs 16 24","book":"1Kgs","c